findings.remediation:
Replace the wildcard policy with least-privilege statements. List only the
actions the workload needs on only the ARNs it touches:
policy = jsonencode({
  Version = "2012-10-17"
  Statement = [{
    Effect   = "Allow"
    Action   = ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject"]
    Resource = ["arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*"]
  }]
})
Use IAM Access Analyzer policy generation from CloudTrail to derive the minimum set.

Enforce IMDSv2 on the instance / launch template:
metadata_options {
  http_endpoint = "enabled"
  http_tokens   = "required"   # IMDSv2 only
  http_put_response_hop_limit = 1
}

Enable detailed monitoring on the EC2 instance (1-minute CloudWatch metrics):
resource "aws_instance" "this" {
  # ...
  monitoring = true
}

Enable deletion protection to prevent accidental destruction:
resource "aws_db_instance" "this" {
  deletion_protection = true
}
For S3, remove `force_destroy = true`. For EC2, set `disable_api_termination = true`.
